good evening we start tonight with a  developing story that we've been  tracking for months  involving jorge gomez thanks for joining  us here at five i'm denise valdez good  evening i'm brian loftis now he is the  man who was shot and killed at a protest  by metro police last year  lawyers for his family say they have new  video showing  officers allegedly using excessive force  oracle mana joining us now live from the  federal courthouse downtown with the  details and also how metro is responding  tonight marco  denise and brian this all stems from a  black lives matter protest  last summer that happened here near the  federal courthouse  where jorge gomez was shot and killed  family attorneys holding a press  conference here earlier today  on what would have been gomez's 26th  birthday  the attorneys say the videos they  released today contradict the account  given by metro police about that chaotic  night  but it's still hard to tell from this  video what exactly happened metro has  said that gomez raised a rifle toward  officers before they shot him 19  times but attorneys claim although gomez  had a gun he did not  point it toward police adding that  openly carrying a gun was his  constitutional right  attorneys further claimed that gomez was  just trying to go home  after the protest lawyers for gomez's  parents filed a civil rights lawsuit  against the officers involved  ryan fryman dan emerton vernon ferguson  and andrew locker and they just added a  fifth officer john sue who they say  fired non-lethal rounds at gomez before  he was killed  what we're alleging is that he's  responsible  he's the one that set this the chain of  events in motion  right he used unnecessary or excessive  force against jorge  he was robbed of his 26th birthday and  every single one after that we won't be  able to give him hugs anymore  and he gave the best hugs in a statement  to 8 news now metro police said in part  quote the surveillance video released  today by the gomez family  appears to be the same video that the  lvmpd gave to the family's council  the video was originally obtained by the  lvmpd and is one piece of evidence that  is being evaluated in the ongoing  investigation  family attorneys also say that they want  clark county district attorney steve  wolfson  to file charges against the officers in  this case  reporting live from downtown las vegas  tonight orgomana 8 news now
 

